/F2 17 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 740 Tm (Spaced Retrieval Practice in Introductory Programming: A Small) Tj
/F2 17 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 718 Tm (Classroom Study) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 692 Tm (Maya Okafor and Daniel Reyes, Department of Computer Science, Example State College) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 660.5 Tm (Abstract) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 643.0 Tm (We test whether spacing short retrieval quizzes over several days helps novice programmers) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 629.5 Tm (remember loop and function concepts better than massing the same quizzes into one sitting.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 616.0 Tm (In a classroom study with 48 students, the spaced group gained an average of 14 points on a) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 602.5 Tm (delayed test, while the massed group gained 6 points. The benefit was largest for questions) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 589.0 Tm (about nested loops. We conclude that low-stakes spaced quizzes are a cheap and effective) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 575.5 Tm (addition to a first programming course.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 548.0 Tm (1 Introduction) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 530.5 Tm (Novice programmers often feel that they understand a concept right after seeing it, and then) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 517.0 Tm (struggle to use it a week later. Retrieval practice, the act of recalling information from) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 503.5 Tm (memory instead of rereading it, is known to improve long-term retention. Spacing the) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 490.0 Tm (practice over time is known to improve it further. Few studies have tested both ideas) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 476.5 Tm (together in a real introductory programming classroom.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 457.0 Tm (Our research question is simple: does spacing retrieval quizzes over days produce better) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 443.5 Tm (delayed-test performance than taking the same number of quizzes in a single sitting? We also) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 430.0 Tm (ask which kinds of questions benefit most.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 402.5 Tm (2 Related Work) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 385.0 Tm (Earlier work in cognitive psychology shows the spacing effect for vocabulary and facts.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 371.5 Tm (Studies in programming education have mostly looked at tools, such as automated feedback,) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 358.0 Tm (rather than at the timing of practice. Our study is closest to classroom experiments that) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 344.5 Tm (vary the schedule of homework, but we use short quizzes that take under five minutes.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 317.0 Tm (3 Method) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 291.5 Tm (3.1 Participants) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 274.0 Tm (Forty-eight students in two sections of an introductory programming course took part.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 260.5 Tm (Students were assigned to the spaced group or the massed group by section, and neither group) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 247.0 Tm (had prior programming experience beyond one week of the course.) Tj
/F2 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 219.5 Tm (3.2 Procedure) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 202.0 Tm (Both groups took four five-question quizzes on loops and functions. The spaced group took) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 188.5 Tm (one quiz every three days, so the quizzes covered twelve days. The massed group took all) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 175.0 Tm (four quizzes back to back on the first day. Each quiz asked students to write short answers) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 161.5 Tm (from memory, and correct answers were shown after each quiz. Twelve days after the last quiz) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 148.0 Tm (of the spaced group, every student took a 20-question delayed test.) Tj
