/F2 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 740 Tm (3.3 Measures) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 722.5 Tm (The main measure was the gain from a pre-test to the delayed test, in percentage points. We) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 709.0 Tm (also scored the nested-loop questions separately, because instructors reported that these) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 695.5 Tm (were the hardest for beginners.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 668.0 Tm (4 Results) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 650.5 Tm (The spaced group gained 14 points on average from the pre-test to the delayed test, compared) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 637.0 Tm (with 6 points for the massed group. The difference was statistically significant. On the) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 623.5 Tm (nested-loop questions the spaced group's advantage grew to 19 points over the massed group.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 604.0 Tm (Students in the spaced group also reported feeling less confident after each quiz than the) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 590.5 Tm (massed group did, even though they remembered more later.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 563.0 Tm (5 Discussion) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 545.5 Tm (The results suggest that the timing of practice matters as much as its amount. Spacing) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 532.0 Tm (forces students to retrieve a concept after they have partly forgotten it, and this) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 518.5 Tm (effortful recall strengthens memory. The lower confidence reported by the spaced group is) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 505.0 Tm (consistent with the idea of desirable difficulties: practice that feels harder can work) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 491.5 Tm (better.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 472.0 Tm (The study has limits. Students were assigned by section instead of at random, the sample is) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 458.5 Tm (small, and we measured memory twelve days after practice rather than at the end of the) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 445.0 Tm (semester.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 417.5 Tm (6 Conclusion) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 400.0 Tm (Short quizzes spaced three days apart produced larger delayed-test gains than the same) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 386.5 Tm (quizzes taken at once. Instructors can adopt this at almost no cost by spreading existing) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 373.0 Tm (practice questions across the week. Future work should use random assignment and a longer) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 359.5 Tm (retention interval.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 332.0 Tm (References) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 314.5 Tm ([1] Example Author. The Spacing Effect in Memory. Journal of Imaginary Learning, 2015.) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 295.0 Tm ([2] Sample Writer. Retrieval Practice for Novices. Proceedings of the Fictional Education) Tj
/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 64 281.5 Tm (Conference, 2018.) Tj
